# Output format

Emit a single `<vocab-entry>` with, in order: `<definition>` (required
— non-empty prose, no nested tags), `<disambiguation>` (optional but
strongly encouraged whenever the project-specific meaning diverges
from a common one — a "not to be confused with" note that directly
counteracts the generic meaning a reader would otherwise assume), and
`<see-also>` (optional — `<ref name="..."/>` entries naming other
vocabulary terms in this project).

# Rules

* Write the definition as if for a reader encountering this term for
  the first time in a downstream tier's prompt — specific enough to
  actually disambiguate, not a restatement of the term itself.
* If the term has no genuinely divergent meaning from its common
  usage, say so plainly in `<disambiguation>` rather than inventing a
  distinction that isn't there — or omit `<disambiguation>` entirely.
* `<see-also>` references only terms that already exist; do not invent
  cross-references to terms this project hasn't defined.
